{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>His brothers.</b> His relatives." "<b>A distance of seven days.</b> All those three days that the informer walked to inform Laban, Jacob walked on his way. The result: Jacob was six days' distance from Laban, and on the seventh Laban caught up with him. We learn that all the distance Jacob traveled in seven days, Laban traveled in one day — as it is said ״וַיִּרְדֹּף אַחֲרָיו דֶּרֶךְ שִׁבְעַת יָמִים״, and it is not said וַיִּרְדֹּף אַחֲרָיו שִׁבְעַת יָמִים."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:29.760918852Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}